     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This dose is double the maximum. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is really what you want, tell me and I'll add a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
